[28.6, "o", "No active code node covers this line (the symbol may have moved or been removed).\r\nQuery docs/adr/001-use-sqlite-default.md:1 → 1 matched file-level decision(s)\r\n\r\n┌─────────────────────────── Decision #1: Use SQLite (stdlib `sqlite3`) as the sto… ────────────────────────────┐\r\n│                                                                                                               │\r\n│  [Location]                                                                                                   │\r\n│    docs/adr/001-use-sqlite-default.md:1                                                                       │\r\n│    binding: file-level decision                                                                               │\r\n│  [Decision]                                                                                                   │\r\n│    Use SQLite (stdlib `sqlite3`) as the store under `.codegraph/graph.db`.                                    │\r\n│  [Reason]                                                                                                     │\r\n│    CodeGraph needs a local store for CodeNodes and Edges during the MVP. Judges and developers must run the   │\r\n│  CLI without operating a database server. Multi-hop graph queries matter later, but day-one reliability and   │\r\n│  zero setup matter more.                                                                                      │\r\n│  [Alternatives]                                                                                               │\r\n│    · Dgraph first (rejected for MVP: requires Docker and ops setup).                                          │\r\n│    · In-memory only (rejected: cannot time-travel after the process exits).                                   │\r\n│  [Source]                                                                                                     │\r\n│    adr · ADR 001-use-sqlite-default                                                                           │\r\n│    author: unknown · date: 2026-10-03                                                                         │\r\n│  [Status]                                                                                                     │\r\n│    ✅ active                                                                                                  │\r\n│  [Constraints]                                                                                                │\r\n│    · Install and demos work offline with no Docker.                                                           │\r\n│    · Schema migrations must be lightweight (`ALTER TABLE` when columns are added).                            │\r\n│    · A different store would be a rewrite of `storage.py`, not a CLI flag — see                               │\r\n│    · ADR-006 for what that costs when the backend does not exist.                                             │\r\n│  [Confidence]                                                                                                 │\r\n│    ★★★★☆  80%                                                                                                 │\r\n│                                                                                                               │\r\n│                                                                                                               │\r\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\r\n"]
